will there be a meatless burger in your  future it's not impossible in 2018 total  sales of substitute meat products were  already estimated to be about 4.5  billion dollars and McDonald's recently  announced that it will test market a  burger that uses plant proteins instead  of beef but going forward companies like  beyond meat may have trouble finding the  dry peas they need to make patties the  good news 1.1 million acres were planted  in 2019 the bad news switching from  traditional crops to dry peas will  involve equipment changes and may  require some farms to gain experience  working with the new crop adding costs  and time and another barrier exists for  companies that insist on using organic  Peas under current USDA rules it takes  three years to qualify land to raise  certified organic crops but it all goes  well plant-based meat sales could double  by 2024 and might account for 20% of all  meat sales in a few decades would you  buy it fast food meatless burger let us  know in our poll also let us know  whatever topics you would like our  scholars to cover in 60 seconds and be  sure to LIKE and subscribe for more  research and videos from AEI
 

